ph’s vertex indices when it has them), unreached ones left out, so the source need not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"come first. Edge positions are the arborescence’s own, in vertex order: edge k leads to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the k-th listed vertex other than the root, counting from 0. The graph’s edge into a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex stays "},{"code":"tree.parentEdge(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". O(n); the vertices are hashed once, into the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arborescence’s lookup table, unless they are the "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s "},{"code":"0..<k","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in order."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"tree.sources.count == 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Several sources make a rooted forest, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Trees has no type for; the source count is the caller’s own argument to the search, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"asking for one root with several is a programming error, not a lookup that may miss.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/Trees","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/Trees\/Arborescence"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths","relatedModules":["Trees"]}],"externalID":"s:5Trees12ArborescenceV13ShortestPathsEyACyxGAD0C8PathTreeVyqd__qd_0_Gc6VertexQyd__Rsz14GraphProtocols08DirectedH0Rd__SLRd_0_r0_lufc","symbolKind":"init","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind